model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Tool-call traffic credits the account branches the framework actually ran, including failed branches, after intersecting evidence with the invocation's authorized account selection. Protocol 35 adds optional account-use evidence without changing older bundles; its served framework pin matches the prepared package, maintained catalog publishers and reproducible source overlays and protocol 34 freezes its OAuth validation. Calls lacking evidence may credit a single selected account but never fan out across several accounts. Counts, failures and last success share this attribution on the Accounts list, app tabs and Details. Existing ambiguous aggregates expire under the unchanged seven-day totals and 31-day history windows; no speculative backfill or storage migration changes saved accounts. An explicitly selected account whose source already failed returns that source failure before selection or observation; only the branch whose operation runs supplies account-use evidence."
    }
  }
}
